What is ansible role?

An Ansible role is a structured way of organizing Ansible playbooks and related files to automate tasks in a reusablenand modular fashion.

Structure of a Role

roles/
└── webserver/
  ├── defaults/
  │ └── main.yml     # Default variables
  ├── files/
  │ └── httpd.conf    # Static files to copy
  ├── handlers/
  │ └── main.yml     # Handlers for services (e.g., restart Apache)
  ├── meta/
  │ └── main.yml     # Role dependencies and metadata
  ├── tasks/
  │ └── main.yml     # Main list of tasks to run
  ├── templates/
  │ └── index.html.j2  # Jinja2 templates
  └── vars/
    └── main.yml     # Variables with higher priority than defaults
